; ted-swapd0bord-index (#384): setdefs takes the colour words of the
; option block unchecked and marks the colour buttons with swapd0bord
; (colour | 4 x group): a value >= 4 from L:blitzeditor.opts selects the
; button of another group, or one behind the 16 buttons (index >= 16:
; bytes behind their borders are swapped).  Options file with normcol 7;
; OPTIONS, OK, QUIT (savedefs).  Correct: TED survives the requester and
; the colour is taken as 0..3 (7 masked: 3), also in the saved options;
; the original keeps 7 (recorded before the fix).  (What the swaps
; damage shows only in pixels or, for values >= 16, in data laid out
; differently in the port: not checked here, review only.)
; @fixed #384
; @source none
; @opts normcol=7
; @expect opts blitzeditor.opts normcol=3
timeout 10
wait req "OKEE DOKEE"
gad 1
wait screen
menu 0 3
wait req "OK" "CANCEL"
gad 26
wait screen
menu 0 9
wait exit
